        en("ui.all.signatures", "All signatures", LanguageSlot.CONTROL),
        en("ui.turn.any.combination.extra", "Turn on any combination. Extra attention sends those signatures, such as body cameras, glasses, recorders, and pentest gear. Payload location sends Remote ID and any radio that advertises its own position. Watchlist sends bookmarked signatures and named radios with Alert on. All signatures sends every labeled radio, and it gets noisy in a crowd. A radio with no signature is never sent. A pin needs a position, from the advertisement or from {gps}.", LanguageSlot.BODY),
        en("ui.how.long.spot.stays", "How long a spot stays", LanguageSlot.CONTROL),
        en("ui.after.radio.leaves.spot", "After a radio leaves, its spot keeps that name for this long. The time starts when it leaves. Until deleted lasts until you turn the feed off. This phone’s own marker still lasts about 2 minutes. Tap a marker for the name, MAC, and signal.", LanguageSlot.BODY),
        en("ui.mark.map.where.phone", "Puts a mark where this phone was, and a line on this phone’s marker. A short hit is a pin. A hit that keeps going while the phone moves is an ellipse from the start to the last place, half as wide as it is long. The mark does not say where the cause is. Off sends nothing. While alerting sends a hit at or above {level}. Red line keeps that line for 10 minutes after the hit, and the ellipse stops growing when the hit ends. Any hit also sends a Low detection that never draws the red line. This phone needs a GPS fix.", LanguageSlot.BODY),
        en("ui.gnss.warnings", "GNSS warnings", LanguageSlot.CONTROL),
        en("ui.how.long.mark.stays", "How long the mark stays", LanguageSlot.CONTROL),
        en("ui.time.starts.last.update", "The time starts at the last update. Until deleted lasts until you set GNSS warnings to Off.", LanguageSlot.BODY),
        en("ui.tak.trusted.note", "A trusted-network warning can mark where this phone was. The mark is this phone, not the access point. Both stay dim until Watch trusted networks is on.", LanguageSlot.BODY),
